//! The node runtime: a tick-driven event loop that makes the assembled [`Node`] actually RUN over a
//! constant-rate onion [`CellChannel`].
//!
//! There is ONE node role and it does EVERYTHING — produce, prove, verify, AND relay. A node is never
//! a passive relay: every node builds the next block from the tips it already holds ([`Node::produce`]
//! → [`crate::dag::Dag::tips`]) and gossips it, so killing all-but-one node cannot stall the DAG (the
//! keystone; a non-producing "relay" node would be exactly the single point of failure this rejects).
//! The only other network role is a PoS **bridge validator**, which is this same running node plus the
//! bonded-finality overlay ([`crate::validator`]) — it still produces + relays.
//!
//! One [`NodeRuntime::tick`] at a given `now_ms`: (1) DRAINS every inbound cell-reassembled message and
//! routes it — a gossiped block is ingested (consensus-validated graft) and, if new, re-gossiped onward
//! (natural dedup: a block/tx already held doesn't re-Add, so it isn't re-sent → no gossip loop); a
//! gossiped tx is admitted to the mempool + re-gossiped; a #29 DSYNC `SyncResponse` is adopted
//! (verify-once → O(1) jump). (2) PRODUCES a block on the target spacing from the tips it holds and
//! gossips it. (3) PUMPS exactly one constant-rate cell (a queued chunk or a cover cell). Driven by
//! explicit `now_ms` so it is deterministic + testable; the live binary drives it from a wall-clock
//! timer. Catch-up from FAR behind is the O(1) #29 DSYNC adopt (one verify → jump to tip). The only
//! catch-up path is BEACON-ADOPT: nodes emit a constant-rate untrusted tip-beacon `(genesis, tip,
//! blue_work)`; a node whose tip is lighter fires ONE #29 DSYNC and adopts the peer's tip via the
//! verify-once ≤1.8MB decider bundle (heaviest VERIFIED tip wins). There is NO block-by-block backfill —
//! an orphaned gossip block is itself treated as a heavier-tip beacon → one O(1) DSYNC jump, never a
//! genesis-to-tip history replay. This makes a persistent chain split impossible (deterministic total
//! order over `(blue_work, id)`, bounded by one beacon interval).

